<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <Title>Stride Community Toolkit - Shapes</Title>
        <Description>Immediate-mode vector shapes for Stride: filled convex shapes whose outline stays a constant few pixels wide at any zoom, distance or window size, because a signed distance function measures it per fragment instead of building it as geometry.

What's inside:
- ShapeBatch, registered with game.AddShapeBatch(): polygons, discs, rings, rounded rectangles, wire boxes, camera-facing billboards, and 3D lines in either a real world-space width or a constant on-screen pixel width, where hardware line rendering clamps to one pixel
- Flat shapes placed anywhere in 3D - on a plane you choose, facing the camera, or swung about an axis - as well as the plain 2D case
- Thousands of shapes per frame in one instanced draw call: no models, materials or assets involved
- ShapeComponent to draw a shape from an entity's transform, so shapes join the component system without needing a model
- Per-shape outline width and fill, and per-batch depth testing for scene decals versus overlay gizmos

Ported from the Box2D testbed's solid_polygon shader (Erin Catto, MIT) and extended to 3D.$(StrideVersionNote)</Description>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <Import Project="..\CommonSettings.props" />

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="Effects\*.*" Pack="true" PackagePath="stride\Effects" />
        <None Include="*.sdpkg" Pack="true" PackagePath="stride" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- This library ships a shader. Shaders are assets compiled by the asset compiler according
             to the Graphics API target, so the package that owns the shader owns the dependency. -->
        <PackageReference Include="Stride.AssetCompiler" Version="$(StrideVersion)" IncludeAssets="build;buildTransitive" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Stride.CommunityToolkit\Stride.CommunityToolkit.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Update="Effects\ShapeShader.sdsl">
            <LastGenOutput>ShapeShader.sdsl.cs</LastGenOutput>
        </None>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>